  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "f3cce0a7-05b7-4440-a183-8acb2e215f59",
      "name": "Sticky Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -1008,
        -16
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 520,
        "height": 1400,
        "content": "## Bridge SMS messages between Android and Slack\n\n### How it works\n\nThis workflow bridges SMS messages between an Android device connected through [Relayion](https://relayion.com) and a Slack channel. Relayion ships natively in n8n's two most recent releases; on older, self-hosted versions, install the community node n8n-nodes-relayion from the Community Hub instead (not available on n8n Cloud). Incoming SMS messages are formatted and posted to Slack, while eligible threaded Slack replies are parsed and sent back as SMS responses. After attempting to send a Slack reply as an SMS, the workflow reacts in Slack to show success or failure.\n\n### Setup steps\n\n- Connect and authorize the Relayion trigger and Relayion send node for the Android device that will receive and send SMS messages.\n- Turn on \"Include Body\" on the Relayion inbound webhook, otherwise the SMS text won't come through and Slack will only show a placeholder.\n- Configure Slack credentials for both the Slack trigger and Slack action nodes, including permissions to read channel messages, post messages, and add reactions.\n- Set the `slackChannelId` value in the Set Slack Channel ID node and separately in the Slack trigger's Channel field. These can't be unified, since the trigger has no upstream node to read from when it fires.\n- Configure the Fetch Slack Thread Messages node with a valid Slack token that can call `conversations.replies` for the target channel.\n- Verify that the Slack message format includes the phone number in a way the extraction code can reliably parse.\n\n### Customization\n\nYou can change the Slack channel ID, adjust the SMS-to-Slack message template, update the phone-number parsing code, or customize the success and failure reactions used for delivery status.\n\nFull setup walkthrough, including inviting the bot to your Slack channel and the Signing Secret requirement, is in the README that came with this template."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
